//                  the grade job's `start` sent at AGENT_AGGREGATE_POLL_PRIORITY, below a fan-in with
//                  work), unless its entry ended (failed, nondeterministic, timeout) or its competition
//                  resolved with nothing left to run its open trials (server/pipeline/fanin-sweep.ts
//                  `ended`, endedRunsToClose): then it closes the run `cancelled`, unpublished; once every trial
//                  is done, the trials manifest (agent-score.ts trialsManifest: the action log, stored
//                  as a blob), the performance (aggregateTrials), the score (score.ts buildScore, cost
//                  and authorship as a grade's) and the run's verdict (record.ts finishRun: finished, or
//                  nondeterministic when a trial is), and the run to publish. Beside the score, never in
//                  it, the run's checks trace (agent-score.ts agentChecksBreakdown of the trials' rows,
//                  `checks` above; stored as record.ts stores a grade's trace, run.trace_sha256), so
//                  result_sha256 is what it is without one: none when no trial's scorer wrote rows, and
//                  none, its reason logged, when they make none (trials scored on other checks, a
//                  checks.json dropped). An entrant's entry (no
//                  house entry, no baseline: standingsHouse, submission.baseline) under a harness that
//                  waives nothing (harness.target waives it: a scripted attacker making no model call of
//                  its own is a legal entry there; so does harness.model_calls: optional, a competition
//                  that does not require model calls: agent-score.ts agentHarnessFloorFacts) is held to the LLM
//                  agent floor (agent-score.ts, the rules' "Each entry is an LLM agent"), each trial's
//                  model calls counted off its stored cassette (gateway/cassette.ts
//                  cassetteModelCalls: completions the model answered using tokens, never a models
//                  listing): a trial whose store would be scored and whose live pass made none scores
//                  0, its store not scored (aggregateTrials handed the entry's facts), and the run's
//                  error names those trials (agentSilentNote, after the nondeterminism note if any); a
//                  run none of whose trials made one is refused instead (agentModelCallRefusal): the
//                  run failed, its error the plain reason (AGENT_NO_MODEL_CALL; for an entry whose
//                  passes ran on no provider key, keylessEntry, the missing keys its bundle serves and
//                  the fix), no score, nobody paged; publish carries it to the entry, whose status shows
//                  the check model_call (server/entries/checks.ts, implied from that error in place of
//                  run_completes). A run
//                  it cannot aggregate is failed and paged on its last attempt, and at once when
//                  aggregateTrials refuses its trials (read only off their stored records, so no retry
//                  can change it: trials still priced on two tables, spend-revision.ts); an entry
//                  cancelled meanwhile cancels it
//                  The gateway (openAgentGateway): masq from the server's config, opened with
//                  masq.ts openMasqBroker; null with MAKEFUN_LLM_GATEWAY off, and then no trial runs.
//                  A pin masq refuses from this host's address is paged as an ALERT at start (its 403
//                  source-pin refusal, openMasqBroker's MasqAdminKeyRefusal problem `source`), naming
//                  the address and the `masq keys admin-sources` fix; the broker is kept, so a pin
//                  fixed on the box is picked up by the next mint, and the trials void and hold as
//                  they always have until then.
//                  sweepStaleSandbox clears a crashed grader's containers and networks at start,
//                  once six hours old: what no resumed trial reaped (`dead grader` above).
//                  The agent/v1 runtime (grader/agent.ts, the gateway's modules, masq, the network
//                  sweep and the isolation probe) is loaded on an agent job's first use (the probe's
//                  module as a trial handler is made), never as this module loads: the kit's command
//                  line bundles this module for its rules (cli/grade-local.ts), and the forwarder's
//                  entry module (gateway/main.ts) runs its main when it is part of a bundle that is run
//   scrape/v1      a scrape entry grades in a heat (contracts/scrape.ts): every entrant, the house baseline among
//                  them, run once a round in an order drawn from a public drand round, each trial timed by the
//                  house launcher behind the recording TLS gateway and judged by the bundle's sealed scorer
//                  (grader/scrape/heat.ts runScrapeHeat, trial.ts, score.ts). A heat is exclusive to its host's
//                  egress: it holds the host's lease (heat.ts acquireScrapeHostLease, a scrape_heat_lease row of this
//                  process's database named for ScrapeWorkerDeps.leaseDir, default scrapeLeaseDirFromEnv:
//                  MAKEFUN_SCRAPE_LEASE_DIR, else <tmpdir>/makefun-scrape-lease), so two grading pods of one egress
//                  never run two heats against it, and a heat finding it held waits before it starts (scrapeEgressQuiet:
//                  queued behind the running one, practice or final). What else the lease keeps off the host is its
//                  scope (ScrapeWorkerDeps.leaseScope, default scrapeLeaseScopeFromEnv: MAKEFUN_SCRAPE_LEASE_SCOPE, else
//                  `host`). It protects two things. The upstream's per-address rate buckets and the pacer's schedule
//                  (heat.ts Pacing), which assume the heat is the address's only caller: kept under both scopes, with
//                  the heat's check of the lease before every trial, its heartbeat, its expiry and its takeover, and an
//                  admin's re-judging taking the lease (server/routes/admin/scrape-holds.ts). And a CPU no other job
//                  shares: under `host` (the default, and production's) every other grade or regrade job of this host
//                  waits before it starts while a live lease is held (scrapeHostQuiet: a program, replay or agent grade,
//                  a scrape L1 regrade), and so does a timing heat (`code heat` below); an agent/v1 trial's job, an
//                  entry's hindsight audit and an eras grade's dev-stress hand themselves on instead, and the chain's
//                  attest and challenge guard start no check (scrapeHostHeldBy: `scrape heat` above, `one entry`
//                  below, grader/dev-stress.ts, server/chain/jobs/attest.ts `host`). Under `egress` none of those wait
//                  or hand on (scrapeHostHeldBy is null, scrapeHostQuiet resolves at once): the CPU is the heat's own
//                  pods' reservation instead, their whole CPU limit requested (runScrapeHeatFor sets heat.ts
//                  ScrapeHeatOptions.reserveCpu, scrape/trial.ts ScrapeTrialOptions.reserveCpu, every trial's entry
