//                  attempt too, its live document left, and completes. An answer that began and ended unread
//                  (judge-call.ts JudgeCallFault.unread: a 200 whose stream was cut or ran out the bound, or a request
//                  silent past JUDGE_ANSWER_STALL_MS; threejs-fps-02's
//                  final lost 8.5 minutes and the 63 calls in flight to one, every 45 minutes or so) gave no verdict, so
//                  the sender sends that call again at once (sendJudgeHeatCalls' resendUnread), at most
//                  JUDGE_HEAT_MAX_SENDS sends in all (the first resend held to the heat's answer bound as the first send
//                  was, the third and last only to 240 s and 60 s: judge-call.ts JUDGE_PAIR_SENDS_MAX), each unread send
//                  kept as the call's faulted spare, never scored; every heat's sender does so, a dev grade's provisional
//                  heat's too, while its run lives: one that ends unread after the run has ended (another call's final
//                  fault, a stop, an abort) is never sent again from it, and the next attempt sends it. A call whose third send ends unread as well is never sent again in that attempt, but
//                  no longer ends it at once: the attempt goes on
//                  sending and settling every call its schedule has planned (the rest of its round: the next round is
//                  planned on that call's verdict, so nothing past the round is sent), keeps none past the unread one,
//                  saves those that answered beside the partial (judgeHeatAsidePath, the aside: under the resume key
//                  and the count of calls kept, a sidecar no older release reads, the partial's bytes untouched), and
//                  hands on to a job sent at once (`hand-on:<job id>:<calls kept>`, at most JUDGE_HEAT_HAND_ONS_AT_ONCE an
//                  hour a phase by its hand-on log, then the slot as above); the next attempt sends the unread call
//                  first and takes each saved call in its place unsent (sendJudgeHeat's `aside`). The heat done, its
//                  key is retired (masq's spend beside the meter: flags logged), the record stored, and each field entry's run written its score built again with its
//                  member's verdict (scoreWithJudge: performance.judge) and run.judge_heat_sha256, in one transaction
//                  held to the result each run had (a run written since retries the job, from the calls kept). A
//                  regrade rebuilds the verdict from that record (grader/regrade.ts judgeVerdictOf), never by calling
//                  a model. A final's CPU work runs off this thread (grader/judge-heat-tasks.ts on server/offthread):
//                  its schedule planned again once a batch (sendJudgeHeatCalls' default, judgeHeatScheduleFor), and
//                  at its end its record built, held once, digested and scored (judgeHeatRecordEnd, sent the calls'
//                  texts the partial writer keeps); a resumed attempt reads its kept partial back once and holds
//                  its calls to the heat (keptJudgeHeat: judgeHeatKeptReadOffThread, judgeHeatKeptCheckOffThread),
//                  parsing back here only the calls it resumes from, in slices; a regrade reads a record back held
//                  once a process (regrade.ts loadHeldJudgeHeatRecord). Once its results are written, a final's or
//                  blind round's attempt puts its sends sidecar beside the record (judgeHeatSendsEnd, the blob
//                  namespace's <xx>/<record sha256>.sends.json): each send's time and outcome and what each send cut
//                  unread billed, read back once from OpenRouter within 10 s, the whole end given up past 15 s
//                  (JUDGE_HEAT_SENDS_END_MS); reporting only, the record never holds it. Only an attempt that finishes
//                  writes one: an attempt that ends (a call cut unread three times, whose third cut is final on OpenRouter,
//                  any fault that ends it, an abort, a hand-on) leaves no document, its sends' times and outcomes
//                  dropped with it; a call sent afresh by the heat's one fault re-send keeps both sendings, the later
//                  marked `again` (JudgeSendTimedT)
//   provisional judge
//                  a judged competition's dev grade that passed its gate plays its artifact against every house
//                  anchor in both orders before it is recorded (withProvisionalJudge; judge-heat.ts's provisional
//                  stage, judgeProvisionalCalls: two calls an anchor; sent as the judge heat's are, up to its share
//                  of the judge pool at once (a seat of its own, as a final's heat takes) and kept in planned order, a
//                  batch's last calls backed up by the
//                  same rule and their other sends kept in memory for the record's spares), on a key of its own
//                  (judge/dev/<n>) minted with no dollar cap: no spend is read, weighed or waited on (the header's
//                  `judge keys`). Its record is stored and linked as run.judge_heat_sha256, and its
//                  score carries the verdict (performance.judge, provisional: its win rate against the anchors),
//                  shown on the dev board and never weighed. A grade the heat cannot judge is recorded unjudged and
//                  says so in the log (no gateway, a judge model with no price, no artifact or one the judge
