//                  A bundle naming a ladder (judge.ladder: grader/judge-ladder-tree.ts readJudgeLadder, beside the judge
//                  directory) plays a v3 heat on it instead: the anchors once each, then its adaptive rounds against
//                  the ladder's members of fixed strength (judge-heat.ts judgeHeatPlannedCalls), rated against them;
//                  every grade plays every adaptive round of the ladder's design. While blind rounds hold the
//                  competition (server/routes/competitions/common.ts blindRoundsHold: blind_rounds on, not resolved),
//                  its entries are judged only in its rounds: a dev grade plays no heat, sends no call and claims no
//                  key, only reads its artifact and checks the judge can read it (the dossier's view too), writes its
//                  entry_artifact row with no record (copy detection holds), and is recorded unjudged (cause
//                  `blind`), saying so in a line of its own; cleared, the sweep's rejudge judges it
//   provisional resume
//                  a provisional heat keeps its calls as each is taken, in planned order, with their spares, in
//                  a file of its entry under the work root (judgeProvisionalPartialPath, the data claim every
//                  grader mounts) on the claim; off it (the judge state the tier's, or handed in: provisionalPartialOf)
