//                  from its first call, once),
//                  under its resume key (provisionalResumeKeyOf: its setup whole, the judges its
//                  plan fixed among it, but the scrutiny line); and as a play ends on the platform's fault, the
//                  calls it settled past the first it could not keep (sendJudgeHeatCalls' `unkept`, as a final's
//                  aside). Its next play under the same key (the plan's fallback at once, on the same judge; the
//                  provisional rejudge's later) takes the kept calls as its own, takes each set-aside call up in
//                  its place unsent while it is the call planned there (`earlier`), and sends only the calls with
//                  no verdict, its schedule planned over them round by round as an unfaulted heat's (one verdict
//                  a call, the first to arrive): its record is the one an unfaulted heat makes. Another judge,
//                  seed, field or artifact is another key, and is judged from its first call; so are kept calls
//                  that are no longer the start of the heat's schedule. Its record stored, or the heat's own end
//                  (too many calls with no verdict), the file is removed. A top-up (`extend`) keeps nothing here.
//                  PROVISIONAL_RESUME_FRUITLESS_MAX (3) plays running that end on the fault with no call settled
//                  that the plays before had not park the heat: paged once (deps.page), its calls kept, and every
//                  later play on this release (judgeReleaseOf: the image's MAKEFUN_COMMIT, which both k8s image
