//                      dataset, seed and Score as the window has them) is kept, so a retry resumes; any other is
//                      graded on eraWindowPlan (its own dataset, the seed phaseSeed(competition key, 'dev', that
//                      dataset's sha256) and the public fail key of it, no final window), two executions byte
//                      equal (grade.ts gradeEntry), and its run_era row and blobs recorded (record.ts recordEra)
//                    - the grade stops at the first window not ranked (failed, timed out, two executions that
//                      disagree, an unmetered cost): that window's outcome is the run's, its own Score the result
//                      (the first such window by key is what score.ts aggregateEras returns)
//                    - otherwise the run's result is aggregateEras over every window's Score (regrade.ts erasResult),
//                      and the run's dataset_sha256, seed, fail key, action log, trace and stderr are the median
//                      window's (the result's performance.eras.rank_window); exec_count and wall_ms are the sums over
//                      the windows, flags the median Score's
//                  A regrade of a run with run_era rows follows them window by window (regrade.ts regradeErasL1,
//                  regradeErasL2): each row's dataset resolved by its unique sha256, its own seed and public fail key,
//                  the regrade's run a run_era row of its own for each. A dev phase without practice_windows, and a
//                  run without run_era rows, take the path they always have.
//
// Harness faults (sandbox, scorer, a dataset the sim refuses) propagate so the job retries, and so
// does a committed fail key that cannot be derived yet (FailKeyUnavailableError, paged: the header's
// `fail key`); a job
// that can never succeed (no bundle, no snapshot, no dataset, a dataset that fails its hashes, a
// stored authorship summary that does not validate, nothing to regrade, an instance bundle whose
// instance does not check, an agent/v1 run its regrade cannot re-derive, a scrape/v1 competition with
// no house baseline, a scrape/v1 L2 regrade) is a PermanentJobError and goes to the dead-letter queue.
// An instance bundle with no instance drawn yet to grade on is the platform's (`not drawn` below).
//
// platform fault   a clmm score whose LVR (fees - costs - hedged PnL) parts from LVR leg by leg by
//                  more than rounding (sim/clmm/metrics.ts ClmmLvrMismatchError, which every clmm
//                  plan's score throws: harnesses.ts clmmPlan, assertClmmLvr) is a fault of the
//                  scorer or the engine, never the entry's, and no retry mends it: the grade or
//                  regrade throws server/jobs.ts PlatformFaultError (a PermanentJobError naming the
//                  entry or run, the phase and both LVRs), so the job dead-letters at once and is
//                  paged as a `dead grade job` (below), and no run is recorded, so nothing is posted
//                  and the entry is never scored on it; the pipeline's grade stage puts the entry
//                  back as it was rather than failing it (server/pipeline/index.ts). The scorer is
//                  GradeWorkerDeps.clmmScorer (default scoreClmmActionLog); the check holds whatever
//                  it is
//
// not drawn        an instance-drawn phase whose instance is not drawn yet is the platform's, never
//                  the entry's: no instance.yaml in the competition directory at all (nothing drawn:
//                  the practice draw writes it), on the final phase no scored draw record yet (no
//                  instance-draw-0.json: the scored round is not drawn), or an instance tree that is
//                  not there at all (the practice instance or trial not drawn yet: `instance`,
//                  `agent/v1` above; a scored one whose trees are gone). Each is an
//                  InstanceNotDrawnError, a PlatformFaultError naming what is not there and the draw
//                  that mends it. No run is recorded. The pipeline's grade stage puts the entry back as
//                  it was and hands the grade job on until the draw is there (server/pipeline/index.ts),
//                  so a grade's is never paged as a `dead grade job` (below) by its handler (one a stage
//                  with no queue could not hand on dead-letters, and the sweep pages it); a wait past
//                  a day (a draw never made, or a competition directory or MAKEFUN_SEALED_DIR that is
//                  not where the draw wrote) pages the admins once, by the pipeline, and the entry
//                  waits on (server/pipeline/index.ts INSTANCE_WAIT_PAGE_MS); a regrade's
//                  dead-letters and is paged as any PlatformFaultError. A practice tree (the dev
//                  phase's instance or trial) that is there but is not instance.yaml's practice draw
//                  (it digests otherwise, its instance digest is another, or it holds what a sealed
//                  tree may not: a draw of an older instance.yaml, or damaged) is an
//                  InstanceNotDrawnError too: the release's practice draw re-draws it in place
//                  (server/competitions/practice-draw.ts drawCommittedPractice), so its dev grades
//                  wait for it. So does an agent/v1 dev phase whose instance.yaml was drawn by another
//                  generator than the stored bundle's (a release between its deploy and its seed:
//                  `re-drawn practice` above). What else is there but does not check (an instance.yaml that cannot
//                  be read or does not check, a draw record chain that does not verify, a scored
//                  tree that is not its record) stays a PermanentJobError
//
// ranked floor     a clmm phase's window is held to its phase's floor of whole blocks of the
//                  harness's interval.block_hours (contracts/clmm-protocol.ts clmmPhaseBlocksIssue):
//                  CLMM_RANKED_MIN_BLOCKS (28) on the final phase, whose board pays the prizes,
//                  CLMM_MIN_BLOCKS (8) on dev; under it the grade or regrade is a PermanentJobError
//                  (harnesses.ts ClmmShortWindowError, its reason naming the phase, the blocks and
//                  the floor)
//
// dead grade job   a grade job that dies for good pages the admins, once per job and attempt: its
//                  GRADE_JOB_DEAD_ACTION row (the system's, subject the submission), written under
//                  the submission row's lock before the line goes out, is what keeps it from being
//                  paged again. Found in two places. The job's own handler as it dies, when it is
//                  handed its job context (GradeJobContext, which the pipeline's grade stage hands
//                  on: a PermanentJobError, or any throw on its last attempt, isLastAttempt). And a
//                  sweep (createDeadGradeJobPager) over the grade jobs pg-boss holds failed that no
//                  row records: one that died outside its handler (refused by the grade stage before
//                  it, expired with its process gone, failed by hand) or whose handler was handed no
//                  context. The forfeit sweep's job reads every one, every 15 minutes (`sweep`,
//                  server/pipeline/index.ts startWorkers); every grade job, before it grades, reads
//                  only those pg-boss failed since its process's last such read began, less
//                  DEAD_GRADE_RECENT_SLOP_MS (`sweepRecent`: a range of pg-boss's job_i16 on (name,
//                  completed_on), never every failed grade job of the queues with an audit probe
//                  each, which was 36.6 s cold on production's replica on 2026-11-16 for no row),
//                  one read at a time a process and at most one a minute (DEAD_GRADE_RECENT_EVERY_MS);
//                  a death older than that, or one a bounded read could not decide, is the forfeit
//                  sweep's. The page
//                  (deps.page, default console.error: a "[grade] ALERT:" line) names the
//                  competition, the entry, the phase, the job, how it died and its last error, and
//                  the admin route that queues it again: a regrade's POST
//                  /api/admin/runs/<run>/regrade, a grade's POST
//                  /api/admin/submissions/<entry>/grade/resend with the dead job's id, which sends it
//                  again under a fresh job id (server/routes/admin/grading.ts registerGradeResend).
//                  A grade's page says before the route what happens next, by the predicate the stuck-entry
//                  sweep sends by (server/pipeline/stuck-running.ts redriveFateOf, redriveNextWords): sent
//                  again by itself, when and which re-drive (an automated final's results waiting for it),
//                  or nothing retries it, and why.
//                  A grade (kind grade) whose last attempt its grader's stop or kill cut (pg-boss's
//                  output for it: server/jobs.ts isRolloutCutOutput) is sent again that way by the
//                  pager itself when it holds the job queue, before its row is written (grading.ts
//                  `automatic resend`: the route's refusals, at most AUTO_GRADE_RESEND_CAP per entry
//                  and phase); its row is then unpaged (why_not, resent_as). Refused or capped, it
//                  pages as any death, saying why it was not sent again.
//                  The sweep also takes a scrape/v1 final's heat job (scrape-heat, not a re-judging)
//                  whose last attempt was so cut, when it holds the job queue: sent again by itself
//                  (grading.ts resendCutHeatJob, at most AUTO_GRADE_RESEND_CAP per phase), else paged
//                  in the "[scrape] ALERT:" words with why not; either way a GRADE_JOB_DEAD_ACTION row
//                  subject the phase (kind heat) decides it. A heat's other deaths its handler pages.
//                  A job held on its entrant's entry secrets (its error opening
//                  ENTRY_SECRETS_UNOPENED_HOLD_REASON: `entry secrets` above) is paged as held, never
//                  failed: the entry waits ungraded, and the fix is the seal private keys that open the
//                  secrets its error names (MAKEFUN_ENTRY_SECRET_SEAL_PRIVATE_KEYS_FILE; on the cluster,
//                  Secret makefun-entry-secret-seal), then the same route (heldGradeJobPage).
//                  An entry that is out (cancelled, or a refusal that stands: a duplicate snapshot or a
//                  committed secret, server/pipeline/publish.ts isRefused) was never to
//                  be graded, nor a practice top-up round once its final's cut is decided (the decided
//                  cut needs it no more): its death is recorded and logged, not paged. A job cancelled while it
//                  ran (a superseded entry's grade: its attempt's signal aborted and its pg-boss row
//                  `cancelled`, as server/jobs.ts counts its outcome) did not die: no row, no page,
//                  a log line. Nor did an attempt that lost its pg-boss claim (its error, or its
//                  signal's abort reason, the claim-lost error down its cause chain: server/pipeline/
//                  index.ts isClaimLost, thrown by `claim before record` above or by the claim watch's
//                  or pg-boss's abort): another attempt holds the job, or pg-boss failed it under this
//                  one, which the sweep then finds by its row; its handler writes no row and pages
//                  nothing, a log line saying why. A row or a sweep that
//                  fails is logged and never fails the job (its own error stands). The row goes
//                  through payouts/audit.ts recordAudit, whose AuditAction names grade.job_dead.
//
// The hindsight-audit job handler (server/jobs.ts PipelineHandlers.hindsightAudit:
// createHindsightAuditHandler; its rules are server/routes/admin/hindsight.ts's, its audit
// grader/hindsight-audit.ts's):
//   sweep {phase_id}    on a drawn sealed window's final phase (its draw attached the phase's dataset:
//                       admin/hindsight.ts drawnFinal) whose grading has settled, one job per audit
//                       target lacking hindsight_clean and per appeal filed with no record yet
//                       (server/jobs.ts hindsightAuditJobId); anything else is a no-op
//   one entry           its latest final grade run (finished, a replay score) audited with auditEntry:
//                       the snapshot materialized as the grader mounts it; the drawn masked window
//                       (the phase's dataset row) as the real window, its digest the run's; the real
//                       run's hello seed and fail key (the run's, else derived again as grading
//                       derives it: phaseFailKey by the phase's scheme, a FailKeyUnavailableError
//                       retried and paged alike, the header's `fail key`) and its stored net PnL; the
//                       env-lane entry secrets the run recorded, re-opened (recordedEnvSecrets, the
//                       header's `entry secrets`: one erased since is a PermanentJobError, one this
//                       grader cannot open a retryable Error, nothing run either way); the
//                       static scan against the drawn source
//                       (the draw's source dataset row) with the dev phase's window as `background`
//                       (its public amounts identify nothing), the index built once per window pair
//                       and kept (buildHindsightIndex), and the entrant's entry wallets and payout
//                       wallet as ignoreAddresses; CHEAT_CHECK.m surrogates per rung (appeal_m on an
//                       appeal); the seeds from one master secret, HKDF-SHA256 of the server secret
//                       (deps.failKeySecret, on either fail-key scheme) over (kind, entry, run,
//                       appeal attempt) (hindsightSeedMaster), so a
//                       retried job rebuilds the same surrogates and an appeal gets fresh ones. The
//                       record must pass checkAuditRecord, then admin/hindsight.ts
//                       recordHindsightAudit keeps it (and, on an audit, records the check). An audit
//                       of a run already recorded, or an appeal with none awaiting its re-run, is a
//                       no-op; what can never succeed (no draw, no finished replay run, an AuditError)
//                       is a PermanentJobError. The audit works in `<work root>/hindsight-<owner>-XXXXXX`
//                       (HINDSIGHT_SCRATCH_PREFIX), named for its job (regradeOwner of the job's id,
//                       the same on each attempt). Before anything else, each attempt removes what an
//                       attempt of the job that died left so named (regrade.ts reapScratch), each path
//                       logged (scratchReapLine). What no attempt comes back for is removed by the
//                       workers' start (server/pipeline/index.ts sweepDeadWork), and only once all
//                       three hold (removeIfDead): no active job on the start's database holds its
//                       owner, no one has touched it for six hours (its newest change, its own or a
//                       direct entry's, older than grader/sandbox/network.ts STALE_AFTER_MS), and no
//                       live process holds it open or as its cwd (processesHolding). One younger, held
//                       or not to be asked about is kept and logged: a job on another database sharing
//                       the work root, or a run handed no job, may still work in it. While a scrape/v1
//                       heat holds this host's lease under the `host` lease scope (scrapeHostHeldBy:
//                       `scrape/v1` above; under `egress` nothing here waits), an audit
//                       runs nothing: once the no-op cases are ruled out it hands its job on to the next
//                       recheck slot (SCRAPE_HOST_RECHECK_MS, server/jobs.ts hindsightAuditWaitJobId),
//                       so no surrogate shares the CPU with a timed heat and none spends its expiry on it.
//                       An attempt stops once its signal aborts (JobContext.signal: pg-boss gives the
//                       attempt up at its expiry, and retries the job): its replays run in a sandbox
//                       bound to the signal (grade.ts stoppableSandbox), so the abort kills the replay
//                       running and no later one starts, and an attempt given up before its audit
//                       materializes nothing. Its scratch is removed as ever, nothing is recorded (not
//                       even a record its audit finished), and it rejects with the signal's reason,
//                       never a PermanentJobError: the retry audits afresh, never beside a first that
//                       goes on replaying, and records once.
//   dead                an entry job that dies for good pages the admins, once per job: its
//                       HINDSIGHT_AUDIT_DEAD_ACTION row (the system's, subject the submission), written
//                       under the submission row's lock before the line goes out, is what keeps a
//                       later sweep from paging the job again. Found in two places. The job's own
//                       handler as it dies (a PermanentJobError, or any throw on its last attempt:
//                       isLastAttempt of JobContext.retryLimit), when the audit's entry is an
//                       unchecked audit target on that run and no newer audit job of the run is held,
//                       or an appeal waits for that re-run. And each sweep, after its sends, for every
//                       unchecked target whose latest audit job pg-boss holds failed, and every
//                       appeal still waiting whose latest re-run job (kind appeal, of the run it
//                       re-runs) pg-boss holds failed (admin/hindsight.ts latestAuditJobOf): one that
//                       died outside its handler, expired with its process gone, or failed by hand.
//                       The page (deps.page, default console.error: a "[hindsight] ALERT:" line) names
//                       the competition, the entry, the run, the job, how it died and its error, and
//                       the fix. A dead audit's: a verdict at POST /api/admin/submissions/<id>/hindsight
//                       (deadAuditOf), given with no audit record, open until the final phase is
//                       finalized (at or after its ends_at too, which the page then says). A dead
//                       appeal re-run's: a verdict deciding the appeal without it, likewise open until
//                       finalize (deadAppealOf past ends_at); its handler pages it only while no newer
//                       re-run job of the appeal is held. Reading or writing a page that fails is
//                       logged, and never fails the job (its own error stands) or the sweep.
//
// The dev-stress job handler (server/jobs.ts PipelineHandlers.devStress) is grader/dev-stress.ts's
// createDevStressHandler, which reads this file's helpers (practiceWindowsOf, storedEraWindows, entryRuntime, regradeOwner,
// scratchReapLine, scrapeHostHeldBy) and which nothing here imports back: the eras dev grade's stress on the kit's shared
// block surrogates, its scratch `<work root>/devstress-<owner>-XXXXXX` (DEV_STRESS_SCRATCH_PREFIX), a scrape/v1 heat
// waited out as an audit's (server/jobs.ts devStressWaitJobId).

